      {
        "id": "ROM.8.30-ROM.9.12",
        "orgId": "ROM.8.30-ROM.9.12",
        "bibleId": "01b29f4b342acc35-01",
        "bookId": "ROM",
        "chapterIds": [
          "ROM.8",
          "ROM.9"
        ],
        "reference": "Romans 8:30-9:12",
        "content": [
          {
            "name": "para",
            "type": "tag",
            "attrs": {
              "style": "p"
            },
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "and whom He foreordained, these also He called; and whom He called, these also He declared righteous; and whom He declared righteous, these also He glorified. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.30",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.30"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "What, then, will we say to these things? If God [is] for us, who [is] against us? ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.31",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.31"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "He who indeed did not spare His own Son, but delivered Him up for us all, how will He not also with Him grant to us all things? ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.32",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.32"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "Who will lay a charge against the chosen ones of God? God [is] He that is declaring righteous; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.33",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.33"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "who [is] he that is condemning? Christ [is] He that died, indeed, rather also, was raised up; who is also on the right hand of God—who also interceded for us. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.34",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.34"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "Who will separate us from the love of the Christ? Tribulation, or distress, or persecution, or famine, or nakedness, or peril, or sword? ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.35",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.35"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "According as it has been written: “For Your sake we are put to death all the day long; we were reckoned as sheep of slaughter.” ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.36",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.36"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "But in all these we more than conquer, through Him who loved us; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.37",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.37"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for I am persuaded that neither death, nor life, nor messengers, nor principalities, nor powers, nor things present, ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.38",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.38"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "nor things about to be, nor height, nor depth, nor any other created thing, will be able to separate us from the love of God that [is] in Christ Jesus our Lord.",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.8.39",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.8.39"
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "para",
            "type": "tag",
            "attrs": {
              "style": "p"
            },
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "Truth I say in Christ, I do not lie, my conscience bearing testimony with me in the Holy Spirit, ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.9.1",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.9.1"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "that I have great grief and unceasing pain in my heart— ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.9.2",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.9.2"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for I was wishing, I myself, to be accursed from the Christ—for my brothers, my relatives, according to the flesh, ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.9.3",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.9.3"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "who are Israelites, whose [is] the adoption, and the glory, and the covenants, and the lawgiving, and the service, and the promises, ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.9.4",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.9.4"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "whose [are] the fathers, and of whom [is] the Christ, according to the flesh, who is God over all, blessed for all ages. Amen. ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.9.5",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.9.5"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "And it is not possible that the word of God has failed; for not all who [are] of Israel are these of Israel; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.9.6",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.9.6"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "nor because they are seed of Abraham [are] all children, but, “in Isaac will a seed be called to you”; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.9.7",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.9.7"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "that is, the children of the flesh—these [are] not children of God; but the children of the promise are reckoned for seed; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.9.8",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.9.8"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "for the word of promise [is] this: “According to this time I will come, and there will be to Sarah a son.” ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.9.9",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.9.9"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "And not only [so], but also Rebecca, having conceived by one—our father Isaac ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.9.10",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.9.10"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "(for they being not yet born, neither having done anything good or evil, that the purpose of God, according to [divine] selection, might remain; not of works, but of Him who is calling), ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.9.11",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.9.11"
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "text": "it was said to her, “The greater will serve the less”; ",
                "type": "text",
                "attrs": {
                  "verseId": "ROM.9.12",
                  "verseOrgIds": [
                    "ROM.9.12"
                  ]
                }
              }
            ]
          }
